                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Matt, I have a few queries/thoughts on this one."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/platform.h",
                    "line": 2710,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I prefer we're more specific here and list the error values along with their intent"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/platform.h",
                    "line": 2710,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Johnston",
                        "email": "matt@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "mkj"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/platform.h",
                    "line": 2715,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I prefer we don't decompose the message this way. Was there some benefit over not defining a struct?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/platform.h",
                    "line": 2715,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Johnston",
                        "email": "matt@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "mkj"
                    },
                    "message": "Not really, will make a struct."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/platform.h",
                    "line": 2715,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Johnston",
                        "email": "matt@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "mkj"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/platform.h",
                    "line": 2729,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "In general I'd prefer the iterator-style approach (which I realise is somewhat tedious to implement), however if we're going to do it this way, then using a struct and a flexible array member with `LIBPLDM_CC_COUNTED_BY` at least helps the compiler catch obvious silliness?\n\nPerhaps `__counted_by_ptr()` would help eventually ( mentioned in https://social.kernel.org/objects/dd64a1d9-bb48-4bed-8a3e-bd1153b83d4a )"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/platform.h",
                    "line": 2729,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Johnston",
                        "email": "matt@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "mkj"
                    },
                    "message": "Given it's limited to 8 items an iterator API might be overkill. (Do you know if composite state sensors are used much?). I'll add a struct."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/platform.h",
                    "line": 2729,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Heh, I should have checked the spec before I commented. Yeah, an iterator is overkill. 8 entries of 2 bytes - I'd make it a fixed-sized array in the struct?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/platform.h",
                    "line": 2729,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Johnston",
                        "email": "matt@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "mkj"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/platform.c",
                    "line": 2526,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Needs a `NULL` check."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/platform.c",
                    "line": 2526,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Johnston",
                        "email": "matt@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "mkj"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/platform.c",
                    "line": 2527,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This can be `pldm_msgbuf_extract(buf, op_state_val);`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/platform.c",
                    "line": 2527,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Johnston",
                        "email": "matt@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "mkj"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/platform.c",
                    "line": 2536,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Is it necessary to use this for the return value? I prefer we use errnos going forward."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/platform.c",
                    "line": 2536,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Johnston",
                        "email": "matt@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "mkj"
                    },
                    "message": "`INVALID_SENSOR_OPERATIONAL_STATE` is listed as a response completion code for SetNumericSensorEnable in the spec, so I thought it would be best to return the most specific error response. Could change it to a generic `-EINVAL` which will get translated to a `PLDM_ERROR_INVALID_DATA` response."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/platform.c",
                    "line": 2536,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, if you could translate it in the caller that would be nice."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/platform.c",
                    "line": 2536,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Johnston",
                        "email": "matt@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "mkj"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
